{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMwByHjRtZDnzjkqKce","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the caching in `bot.py` and written up the details in `ANSWER.md`. It's tested only against an offline simulation of the cache rules, not the real API, so check `logs/usage.jsonl` after it runs for real.\n\n**Cause:** the whole system prompt (instructions, profile and facts) was sent as one cached block. A cache hit needs an identical prefix, so adding a fact changed the block and the entire ~1,000-token prompt was written to cache again. That happened in the tool-loop round right after each `save_fact`.\n\n**Why I didn't just add a cache marker after the instructions:** the tools plus instructions come to about 945 tokens (worked out from your log, where a request with no facts cached exactly 1,024). Sonnet 4.5 won't cache anything shorter than 1,024 tokens, so that marker would be ignored without any error.\n\n**What I changed** (`build_system` in `bot.py`):\n- **New layout:** the first block holds the instructions plus the athlete's date, name, sport, zones, goal and language. After it comes one block per fact, with the cache marker on the last fact.\n- **Why it works:** facts are only ever appended, so the new prompt is the previous one plus one block. The API finds the entry the previous call saved, reads it, and writes only the new fact (about 5–15 tokens). After a `save_fact` you should see roughly `cache_read ≈ 1050, cache_creation ≈ 15` instead of `0 / ≈1100`.\n- **Small reorderings:** `Language:` moved above the facts, and the `- (none yet)` placeholder became a note in the facts header. Anything that changes after the facts would break the \"old prompt is a prefix of the new one\" property.\n- **Date kept in the cached part:** it changes once a day, and a 5-minute cache never lasts overnight anyway. Without it, a new athlete with no facts would drop below the 1,024 minimum.\n\n**Checked:** the simulation (kept in `/tmp`, outside the repo) ran `reply()` with scripted `save_fact` calls. Every call after the first read the full prompt from cache, and calls after a save wrote only 5–6 tokens.\n\n**Limits:**\n- I left the keyword tool filtering alone, as `NOTES.md` asks. Messages that pull in the planning or race tools still get their own separate cache entry; that's unrelated to memory writes.\n- The fix only works while facts stay append-only. If you later add editing, deleting or capping of facts, the call after such a change does one full write, then caching goes back to normal.\n\nI also updated the caching paragraph in `README.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1763,"cache_read_input_tokens":39565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1763},"output_tokens":703,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd7237aa-2eba-4c9d-bc7d-845ce2c53722","uuid":"77e52ef0-ece9-4a51-bf4a-3d927a52e1e3","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:32:16.201Z","request_id":"req_011CgEMwBiQLVPc821Mv1d5d"}
